# Normalize every text file to LF in the repository AND in the working tree.
#
# Without this, Git for Windows' default `core.autocrlf=true` checks the tree
# out with CRLF endings, which Prettier (endOfLine: "lf", its default) then
# reports as a formatting error in every file — so `npm run format:check`,
# a CI gate, fails on a clean clone for every Windows contributor and buries
# real formatting problems in the noise. `eol=lf` pins the working-tree
# ending regardless of each developer's autocrlf setting.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary files Git must never touch.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary

# Generated — keep it out of diffs and language stats.
package-lock.json -diff linguist-generated=true
